  "scientific_attribution_limits": [
    "Adaptive128 versus previous256 changes nonuniform edges and Chebyshev phasor simultaneously; previous256 uses Taylor. It also changes CE-fast endpoint skipping/deferred cache, source revision and H200 versus H100 hardware. These preserve the intended target but can change floating-point and sampler trajectories.",
    "Both recent runs use the exact same final source frequency prefix and the same training/verification-bank hashes. Their model grid approximations differ, so matching scientific configuration is not proof of identical approximate likelihoods everywhere.",
    "The older1024 runs predate batched network evaluation, share the same noise and intended physical model, and use Taylor with 21 anchors. Their explicit source-frequency prefix is not recorded; their sparse waveform grid differs from the 2048-derived prefix frozen in the recent runs. Do not infer prefix equality from the native-grid prefix.",
    "Attempts5 and8 use the same configuration and seed; attempt8 enables a private sweep scan through its execution launcher. They are not independent-seed replications. Their changed production files are nss.py and swig.py, as confirmed by manifests.",
    "All runs keep 4096 live points, eight sweeps, 96 slices, stepping-out, max expansions 10, max shrinkage 100, termination_dlogz 0.0485873516, and the same priors/physical coordinates. Equal RNG seeds do not ensure identical draws after numerical or control-flow changes.",
    "Finite training, verification and three native-grid checks are not prior-wide, posterior-wide or absolute-evidence certification. Posterior overlays and distribution summaries are empirical consistency checks; distinguish Monte Carlo variation, mixing and approximation changes.",
    "The current same-machine fixed256 Taylor run timed out and has no completed posterior; it cannot replace the completed historical comparator.",
    "Whole preflight analysis/config hashes differ because heterodyne and sampler implementation controls are included. These hash mismatches do not indicate different PSDs, injection or priors; semantic equality was checked separately."
  ],
